BearSSL for sbhttp (starbite/wifi/http.c): TLS 1.2 client with X.509 checks.

Source: https://www.bearssl.org/git/BearSSL, commit 7bea48e5e850ab4cafbe68d3765cdaba13a86d6f (the same
pin as xnu/series-*/0020-stage-bearssl.sh). MIT licence (LICENSE.txt). Unmodified files.

Only what a client built with br_ssl_client_init_full() links is kept: the files listed in FILES (found
from a GNU ld map of an aarch64 link of http.c + tls/ta.c against all of BearSSL), all of inc/, and
src/inner.h and src/config.h. FILES.test: what only the host test adds (x509_decoder.c: the test CA
made into a trust anchor at run time). To refresh: fetch the commit into build/bearssl-src, link again, copy.

Built with: -DBR_USE_URANDOM=0 -DBR_USE_UNIX_TIME=0 -DBR_USE_GETENTROPY=0 -DBR_RDRAND=0 (no OS
randomness or clock: sbhttp injects a seed and sets the time from the OS's NTP-checked clock).
